     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div style=\"word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\">You can also check out gridExtra as a package that allows you to combine ggplot2 objects and display them in rows or columns. Although by my experience cowplot works better, it lets you align plots’ axes (something I often need and I’ve never understood how to do with gridExtra).<div><br></div><div><div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none;word-wrap:break-word;line-break:after-white-space\"><div>Lorenzo</div></div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n<div><br><blockquote type=\"cite\"></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
